          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            Given a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+ring"} commutative ring
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            and an
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associative+algebra"} associative algebra
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring"} ring
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphism"} homomorphism
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R \longrightarrow A
            %em Amitsur complex
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Moore+complex"} Moore complex
            of the dual
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cech+nerve"} Cech nerve
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Spec
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi Spec
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spec(A) \to Spec(R)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+complex"} chain complex
            of the form
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                  %mo →
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi A
                  %msub
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi R
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi A
                  %msub
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi R
                  %mi A
                  %msub
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi R
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi ⋯
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  R \to A \to A \otimes_R A \to A \otimes_R A \otimes_R A \to \cdots
          %p
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differentials"} differentials
            given by the alternating sum of the coface-maps.
          %p
            (See also at
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sweedler+coring"} Sweedler coring
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+Hopf+algebroid"} commutative Hopf algebroid
            and at
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Adams+spectral+sequence"} Adams spectral sequence
            for the same or similar constructions.)
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#descent_theorem Descent theorem
          .num_theorem
            %h6#theorem Theorem
            %p
              %strong (descent theorem)
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \to B
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/faithfully+flat"} faithfully flat
              then its Amitsur complex is
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exact+sequence"} exact
          %p
            This is due to (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck"}> Grothendieck
            ,
            = succeed "1)" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/FGA"} FGA
          %p
            The following reproduces the proof in low degree from
            %a{:href => "#Milne"} Milne, prop. 6.8
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p We show that
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 0
                    %mo →
                    %mi A
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mi f
                    %mi B
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mrow
                        %mn 1
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mi id
                        %mo −
                        %mi id
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mn 1
                    %mi B
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi A
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    0 \to A \stackrel{f}{\longrightarrow} B \stackrel{1 \otimes id - id \otimes 1}{\longrightarrow} B \otimes_A B
            %p
              is an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exact+sequence"} exact sequence
              if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi A
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon A \longrightarrow B
              is
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/faithfully+flat"} faithfully flat
            %p
              First observe that the statement follows if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \to B
              admits a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/section"} section
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi s
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mi B
                      %mo →
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s \colon B \to A
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi B
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi A
                    %mi B
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    k \colon B \otimes_A B \longrightarrow B
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi b
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ⊗
                    %msub
                      %mi b
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ↦
                    %msub
                      %mi b
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi s
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi b
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    k \;\colon\; b_1 \otimes b_2 \mapsto b_1 \cdot f(s(b_2))
                    \\,.
            %p This is such that applied to a coboundary it yields
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi b
                    %mo −
                    %mi b
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi s
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo −
                    %mi b
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    k(1 \otimes b - b \otimes 1) = f(s(b)) - b
            %p
              and hence it exhibits every cocycle
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi b
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b
              as a coboundary
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi b
                      %mo =
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi s
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi b
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b = f(s(b))
            %p So the statement is true for the special morphism
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi A
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    B \to B \otimes_A B
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi b
                    %mo ↦
                    %mi b
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    b \mapsto b \otimes 1
            %p because that has a section given by the multiplication map.
            %p
              But now observe that the morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi A
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B \to B \otimes_A B
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product"} tensor product
              of the morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              with
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
              over
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \to B
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/faithfully+flat"} faithfully flat
              by assumption, hence that it exhibits
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
              as a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/faithfully+flat+module"} faithfully flat module
              over
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              means by definition that the Amitsur complex for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi A
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (A \to B)\otimes_A B
              is exact precisely if that for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \to B
              is exact.
          %h3#as_a_bar_construction As a bar construction
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ϕ
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi B
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi \colon B \longrightarrow A
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphism"} homomorphism
            of suitable
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoids"} monoids
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunction"} adjunction
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extension+of+scalars"} extension of scalars
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ⊣
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \dashv
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/restriction+of+scalars"} restriction of scalars
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categories+of+modules"} categories of modules
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %msub
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi B
                  %mi A
                  %mo ⊣
                  %msup
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msub
                    %mi Mod
                    %mi A
                  %mover
                    %munder
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi ϕ
                          %mo *
                    %mover
                      %mo ←
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %msub
                          %mo ⊗
                          %mi B
                        %mi A
                  %msub
                    %mi Mod
                    %mi B
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  ((- )\otimes_B A \dashv \phi^\ast )
                  \\;\colon\;
                  Mod_A
                  \\stackrel{\overset{(-)\otimes_B A}{\leftarrow}}{\underset{\phi^\ast}{\longrightarrow}}
                  Mod_B
                  \\,.
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bar+construction"} bar construction
            of the corresponding
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monad"} monad
            – the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+monadic+descent"} higher
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monadic+descent"} monadic descent
            objects – is the corresponding Amitsur complex.
          %p
            (e.g.
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Hess10"} Hess 10, section 6
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Adams-Novikov+spectral+sequence"} Adams-Novikov spectral sequence
          %h2#references References
          %p The Amitsur complex was introduced in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Shimshon+Amitsur"}> Shimshon Amitsur
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Simple algebras and cohomology groups of arbitrary fields
              %p
                Vol. 90, No. 1 (Jan., 1959), pp. 73-112 (
                %a{:href => "http://www.jstor.org/stable/1993268"}> JSTOR
                )
          %p His results were simplified in
          %ul
            %li
              Alex Rosenberg and Daniel Zelinsky,
              = succeed "," do
                %em On Amitsur’s complex
          %p The statement of proof the descent theorem for the Amitsur complex is due to
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alexander+Grothendieck"}> Alexander Grothendieck
              ,
              = succeed "1" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/FGA"} FGA
          %p A review of the proof in low degree is in
          %ul
            %li#Milne
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/James+Milne"}> James Milne
              , prop. 6.8 of
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lectures+on+%C3%89tale+Cohomology"} Lectures on Étale Cohomology
          %p
            Discussion from the point of view of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sweedler+corings"} Sweedler corings
            and a full proof of the descent theorem is in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tomasz+Brzezinski"}> Tomasz Brzezinski
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Robert+Wisbauer"} Robert Wisbauer
              = succeed "," do
                %em Corings and Comodules
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://www.math.uni-duesseldorf.de/~wisbauer/corinerr.pdf"} errata pdf
          %p
            Disucssion from the point of view of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+monadic+descent"} higher monadic descent
            is in
          %ul
            %li#Hess10
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kathryn+Hess"}> Kathryn Hess
              , section 6 of
              %em A general framework for homotopic descent and codescent
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1001.1556"}> arXiv:1001.1556
              )
          %p
            Discussion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+completion"} formal completion
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C1%29-modules"} (infinity,1)-modules
            in terms of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/totalization"} totalization
            of Amitsur complexes is in
          %ul
            %li#Carlsson07
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gunnar+Carlsson"}> Gunnar Carlsson
              ,
              %em Derived completions in stable homotopy theory
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0707.2585"}> arXiv:0707.2585
              )
